7g9|n|p. p. of Be; -- used for been. ; An insect of the order Hymenoptera, and family Apidae (the honeybees), or family Andrenidae (the solitary bees.) See Honeybee. ; A neighborly gathering of people who engage in united labor for the benefit of an individual or family; as, a quilting bee; a husking bee; a raising bee. ; Pieces of hard wood bolted to the sides of the bowsprit, to reeve the fore-topmast stays through; -- called also bee blocks.	a:1syf,102,1;55t,77,4~55t,77,4;1syf,102,1	n:2h0d,103,3~2h0d,103,3	N:f3f,134,5;274c,103,5~f3f,134,5;274c,103,5
